ng Form Given Only One Eigenvalue" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129136 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129136 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "148c97a4-24c1-5289-ad80-bee4af34509b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186367561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186410856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186572149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1039 "Converting a Matrix to Rotation-Scaling Form Using the Complex Conjugate" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186129033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129214 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "88f3ba21-6407-503e-aec0-fa4462a69e73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1045 "Reducing Real 2x2 Matrices to Rotation-Scaling Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186129976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129361 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9eb9ab54-1ec4-5368-a2e1-150d6811c312" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129717 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129717 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129717 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129717 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\text{i} \\\\ 2+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1+6\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186129717 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53d94693-fca2-5635-a557-72030e989666" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129717 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\ne C,\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=1-6\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i} \\\\ 2-3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186129976 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129976 #edb/ref 1061 20167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129976 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "19750f8a-a131-5f4c-9488-2c2c664f3b38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129976 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129977 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129977 #edb/ref 1061 20168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129977 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e7048fe4-4391-5227-903b-216c1855d7e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129977 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129978 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129978 #edb/ref 1061 20169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129978 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6e5f25d2-d5e2-5abe-a1c6-08572dd50606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129978 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129979 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129979 #edb/ref 1061 20170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129979 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b2e60b35-aad7-5404-bbeb-360484d2e855" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129979 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129980 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129980 #edb/ref 1061 20171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129980 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "380e2b24-5a1b-580a-9d3e-20419aa321c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129980 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129981 #edb/ref 1061 20172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129981 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ed8aecde-9d1f-5061-afa2-aa5cc7c1036e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129981 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130109 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130109 #edb/ref 1061 32487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130109 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7ce1fcbb-0bb6-5b74-ba7c-4006f8e5f481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130109 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130353 #edb/ref 1064 "Rotation-scaling matrices are involved in an important theorem regarding complex eigenvalues.\n\nTo sketch out the key idea, let's consider the matrix \n\n![](images/06/06a28b9b9d8db65a4214ed1d446c68f288978acc59afd3720873da7f825efe13.svg)\n\nwhich has the complex eigenvalue \n\n$$\n\\lambda=1-2\\textrm{i}={\\color{blue}1}+({\\color{red}-2})\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding complex eigenvector \n\n![](images/1b/1b7aa45404b3e6e02cb9802da371f6c74f6848f4b5601261f2257e12b7d362d0.svg)\n\nNow, we construct a rotation-scaling matrix $C$ using the real and imaginary parts of the eigenvalue $\\lambda$ as follows:\n![](images/0f/0f29362b05dd18b6a8a307f531cea6d59c083301703285bde41a9488f228c386.svg)\nWe also construct a matrix $P$ whose columns are the real and imaginary parts of the corresponding eigenvector:\n![](images/d1/d1b2efc5b22e34c0bb4cb93a4777c8d8139ca0047253b7177bd1809a272f5b37.svg)\n\nThe **rotation-scaling theorem** states that $A$ can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\nA=PCP^{-1}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet's check that this is true in this case:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PC{P}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130353 #edb/ref 1065 3594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130353 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d79a993f-cb2c-5ec9-a24b-ddc7bd94485d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130353 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130354 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's now formally state the rotation-scaling theorem:\n\n*Let $A$ be a $2 \\times 2$ matrix with real entries. If $\\lambda$ is a complex (not real) eigenvalue of $A,$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ is an eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda,$ then *\n\n$$\nA = PCP^{-1}\n$$\n\n*where*\n![](images/74/74b63ce33cfa7779a6668a22974b709d549843a221c3b13067887e8193c6e6f0.svg)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When two matrices $A$ and $C$ are related via the equation $A = PCP^{-1},$ we say that they are **similar.**\n\n- The rotation-scaling theorem tells us that every $2 \\!\\times\\! 2$ real matrix with complex (non-real) eigenvalues is similar to a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\n- We call the right-hand side of $A = PCP^{-1}$ the **rotation-scaling form** of $A.$ We can also refer to this as the **rotation-scaling decomposition** of $A.$\n\n- The matrix $P$ *must* be constructed from the eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue defined by $C.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130354 #edb/ref 1065 3595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130354 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "09a26114-9068-50b4-897e-76504d4f7e68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130354 #edb/ref 1067 "The Rotation-Scaling Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130355 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose $A$ is a real $2\\!\\times\\! 2$ matrix. To interpret the rotation-scaling form $A=PCP^{-1},$ we should bear in mind the following:\n\n- The matrix $C$ rotates vectors $\\mathbf x\\in\\mathbb R^2$ and then scales them.\n\n- We can think of $P$ as representing the following change of variable:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = P\\mathbf u \\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow\\qquad  \\mathbf u = P^{-1}\\mathbf x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ can be thought of as a change of variable from $\\mathbf x$ to $\\mathbf u,$ followed by a rotation and scaling before returning to the original variable.\n\n![](images/ab/ab40869137296cea63fe209a842a4713fcae4fbf53c5089e6722b70bdf3f3230.png)\n\nFor example, let's consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n![](images/74/74c17c58d6b39ff6a13ec56e135ec17ce0f260d2e9d90e562544637f6e677db0.svg)\n\nThis is a real matrix with complex eigenvalues and is thus similar to a rotation-scaling matrix. \n\nUsing the techniques described in this lesson, we can show that the rotation-scaling decomposition of $A$ is\n\n![](images/15/1542ac2d3f79e1494ecf9e67dda3219966efdf76267ebda82d7689555dc4df30.svg)\nThe matrix $C$ can be written explicitly as a constant multiple of a rotation matrix as follows:\n![](images/f0/f0d562472e2b230a0cd393829ab4a5dec380e6fd1e2a797af4f1f651aae88f75.svg)\n\nThus, the matrix $C$ represents the following:\n\n- a rotation of $\\arccos\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt 3}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac\\pi 6$ counterclockwise about $O,$ and\n\n- an enlargement of scale factor ${\\color{blue}{2}}.$\n\nThe image of a unit square centered at the origin under the action of $A$ can therefore be decomposed as follows:\n\n![](images/92/92f2ab84b9ac8f36a93c42bf93b70b08a3e64eb3920a8bd2d5276217d936ab79.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130355 #edb/ref 1065 3596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130355 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5e77afe5-c30a-56bd-95a6-037f1a903eda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130355 #edb/ref 1067 "The Geometric Interpretation of Rotation-Scaling Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324543 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186324543 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324543 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46f96ed3-70f8-5ddc-acb6-71587e72f101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324914 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186324914 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324914 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71e88fc2-600f-5365-8aff-acc2b54dc6a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325196 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186325196 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325196 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "90374c3c-03f1-5264-a569-174dfb35f325" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325420 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186325420 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325420 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa418aef-76d7-5108-ab92-460aa075c2f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326143 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186326143 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326143 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f69e55ee-410c-52db-978f-37052ef96cd8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186326143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186324543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326233 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "05c656fc-b22b-5e23-846d-595499735480" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392266 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392266 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392266 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392266 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1+2\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392266 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3f1bb626-14db-51ca-a15c-04bb2468d62d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392266 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392267 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "90d04520-0124-5203-a746-6e09d2550e03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392268 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392268 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392268 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9e0e53bd-8745-5da4-abb6-0168c5f3b7d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392269 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392269 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392269 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "476bc4f8-15ca-5f43-b421-6be5db9f13ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392270 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392270 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392270 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e73dd85-d5f3-51a5-becd-e240b1df303b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392271 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1