/ref 1069 "q-99410" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572149 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572149 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}1+4\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2-5\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572149 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "80ffb1ef-2b1d-5387-91a1-65dcd637622b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572149 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\ne C,\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=2+5\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-4\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572152 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572152 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140502" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572152 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572152 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ -10 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above.\nGiven that $A$ has the complex eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2-5\\text{i},$ and that $A=PC{P}^{-1}$ where $C$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, what is the value of \n$\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572152 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d87763f-3e1e-5f56-b2a4-bc97bccd7687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572152 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nSince we are given the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2-5\\text{i},$ we can immediately construct the rotation-scaling matrix:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,{\\lambda }_{1}=-2-5\\text{i},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ -10 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2-5\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5+5\\text{i} & 5 \\\\ -10 & 5+5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}(-5+5\\text{i}){x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -10{x}_{1}+(5+5\\text{i}){x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables as the free variable. For example, from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\text{i}){x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\text{i}){x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=2$, we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can construct the matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}=\\frac{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572208 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572208 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "15c2ddcb-4a6a-5d10-92a7-7eac543f5050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572208 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572239 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "66c2fbfa-b746-5325-80be-b35737eb36eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572239 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572245 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572245 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7e9b9df9-0488-568f-a29f-8082f11cab44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572245 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572273 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572273 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ed8df2a4-c822-5ea5-aa21-e1c6c89fb344" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572273 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572279 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572279 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f872b89c-4ebf-575b-acff-0457891853a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572279 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186392266 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
